# Local Graphify

Graphify is local code analysis (`graphify` / package `graphifyy`). Cloud URL, MCP, and sending sources out are forbidden.

Default: `graphify extract . --code-only` from the project root you are analyzing. Do not set `--out`, model flags, `--mode deep`, or API keys.

If `graphify` is missing, do not build the graph and do not install it via script. Read files and say there is no graph. Do not run `graphify install --project` in core: it can overwrite team skills.

If `graph.json` exists, for an unfamiliar area run `graphify query` / `path` / `explain` / `affected` first, then read specific lines. Skip for one known file.

Put the real `graph.json` path in code-search subagent prompts; forbid reading the whole file. INFERRED edges are not source facts.

After editing code in that area, run `graphify update .` without a model. Do not require `GRAPH_REPORT` or wiki (community naming may call a model).

Graph lives at `graphify-out/graph.json` in that project root. Not under `.cursor/`. Do not add the catalog to Git.
